\f1\fs22 Two stagehands were loading a nativity scene into a truck and bashed Joseph\'92s head on the door. The production manager wondered whether the set designer hadn\'92t slipped the crew a few shekels to destroy the whole ensemble of figures. He wouldn\'92t have blamed them\'97the Three Wise Men looked like Alexander with different beards, Joseph looked like their clean-shaven father and Baby Jesus looked like a shaved koala with beady Alexander eyes, blunt Alexander nose, and round Alexander ears.\
As for Mary\'97the production manager could not even form the syllables of the name of the person Mary looked like. The blonde hair alone was borderline blasphemy. Since when was the Blessed Mother a Viking? And since when did she have calves like that?\
Last to load were water tanks and the fibreglass containers that looked like rounded oversized coffins for boating enthusiasts.\
Alexander watched the truck doors shut, the drivers climb in, and the whole convoy roll out of the studio\'92s loading yard.\
\'93Who\'92d have thought it would take so many trucks?\'94 he muttered to himself.\
The rest of the crew climbed into a bus. Against advice, Alexander chose to save himself a good couple of hours and travel up to Sublime Point by hover-copt. What was the point of having a hover pad at his mountain home if he didn\'92t use it? His PA had explained that his life insurance would not cover the trip, so Alexander pulled a few strings and borrowed one of his mother\'92s Shakti Enterprises vehicles. That seemed to settle the whole kerfuffle down\'97it, at least, would stay in the air longer than a chicken that had been stuffed, roasted and shot out of a t-shirt cannon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

